-- title:
--   Transport of the two-chart integral model along an R-algebra isomorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $F$ and $F'$ be fields equipped with $R$-algebra structures, and let $j \in F$, $j' \in F'$ be nonzero. Let $e \colon F \to F'$ be an isomorphism of $R$-algebras with $e(j) = j'$. Here `chartAlgFin R F j` is the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j$, `chartAlgInf R F j` is the analogous subalgebra of elements integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$, and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout in schemes of the two morphisms `fFin R F j` and `fInf R F j`, these being `Spec` applied to the algebra inclusions `inclFin R F j` and `inclInf R F j` of the overlap algebra into the two chart algebras; `toBase R F j` is the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ obtained from the structure maps of the two chart algebras by the pushout property. The assertion is that there exist an isomorphism of schemes $w$ from [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) to [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F' j'`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) and $R$-algebra homomorphisms $e_{\mathrm{Fin}} \colon$ `chartAlgFin R F j` $\to$ `chartAlgFin R F' j'` and $e_{\infty} \colon$ `chartAlgInf R F j` $\to$ `chartAlgInf R F' j'` such that $e_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ and $e_{\infty}$ are restrictions of $e$, in the sense that the image in $F'$ of $e_{\mathrm{Fin}}(x)$, respectively $e_{\infty}(x)$, equals $e(x)$; that $w$ is a morphism over the base, i.e. $w.\mathrm{hom}$ followed by `toBase R F' j'` equals `toBase R F j`; and that the two chart squares commute: `Spec.map` of $e_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ followed by `ιFin R F j` equals `ιFin R F' j'` followed by $w.\mathrm{inv}$, and likewise with $e_{\infty}$, `ιInf R F j` and `ιInf R F' j'`. The chart maps $e_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, $e_{\infty}$ are asserted only as $R$-algebra homomorphisms, not as isomorphisms.
--
--   This is the transport-of-structure (functoriality) statement for the two-chart integral model: an $R$-algebra isomorphism of the ambient fields matching the distinguished parameters induces an isomorphism of the associated glued integral models over $\operatorname{Spec} R$, compatible with the two chart immersions. It is the basic input for constructing automorphisms and descent data on the Deligne–Rapoport-style model, and is used by the downstream results producing isomorphisms over the base together with chart-level algebra maps and involutions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_exists_iso_of_algEquiv_apply_eq.lean

import Mathlib
